KR-MCSCF CAS(6,4) of water (STO-3G, X2C) in real, complex and quaternion
symmetry (NZ = 1, 2, 4). Regression test for the fixes of the quaternion
(C1) KR-MCSCF code (Nov 2026); not a test of a well-chosen active space.

Symmetric water: the converged HF coefficients of the C2v run are written
in C1 format (.ACMOUT) and read (.ACMOIN, no SCF) by the C2 and C1 runs,
so that all three start from the same orbitals and give the same energy.
Note: with this (unbalanced) active space the symmetric solution is only
a saddle point in C1 (a symmetry-broken solution is 7.5 mEh lower); the
C1 run stays on it because the start orbitals are exactly symmetric.

Asymmetric water (all atoms in the xz plane, unequal OH bonds): same for
Cs (complex) and C1. The Cs orbitals carry general complex phases, which
exposed errors invisible with the near-real orbitals of a C1 SCF.
